{"body":"**\u003csub\u003e\u003csub\u003e![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/sub\u003e  Avoid tracking the consumer manifest as a generated file**\n\nAfter a full apply to an existing React project, this serializes the checksum of the entire `package.json` into preset state. Any subsequent legitimate consumer edit—such as adding a script or dependency—changes that checksum, so the next full `uifn apply` reaches `planFileChanges` and returns `UIFN_REGISTRY_DIRTY_CONFLICT` instead of merging dependencies again. Exclude the consumer-owned manifest from preset-managed hashes or track only the fields owned by UIFn.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.","line":281,"path":"uifn/registry/src/preset/project.ts"}
{"body":"**\u003csub\u003e\u003csub\u003e![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/sub\u003e  Refuse to overwrite an untracked theme file**\n\nOn the first full apply to an existing project, `tracked` is empty, so an existing `src/uifn-theme.css` with different contents bypasses this conflict check and is scheduled as an update. This silently destroys a consumer-owned file even though the workflow is advertised as safe; an existing target without a matching managed hash should be treated as a conflict rather than assumed to be owned by UIFn.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.","line":213,"path":"uifn/registry/src/preset/project.ts"}
{"body":"**\u003csub\u003e\u003csub\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/sub\u003e  Include source artifacts in new-directory dry runs**\n\nWhen `--dry-run` targets a directory that does not yet exist and the preset uses `installMode: source`, this early return occurs before `planInstall`, so `plan.files` omits every component source file plus `.uifn/registry.lock` and `.uifn/selected-components.json` that the real invocation will write. This makes the dry-run plan materially different from the transaction it is supposed to preview; source-mode planning should still resolve and report all artifact changes without creating the destination.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.","line":263,"path":"uifn/registry/src/preset/project.ts"}
{"body":"On the first full `apply`, `tracked[relativePath]` is absent, so an existing, differing `src/uifn-theme.css` falls through as an `update` and is overwritten. Fail closed for pre-existing unmanaged outputs while keeping intentional merge targets such as `package.json` separate.\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\u003csummary\u003eTechnical details\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n````markdown\n# Preserve unmanaged consumer files\n\n## Affected sites\n- [`uifn/registry/src/preset/project.ts:198-224`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/75018c0db87b5b237eb375e78764a2ff3b2b67e1/uifn/registry/src/preset/project.ts#L198-L224) — a differing file is rejected only when a previous managed hash exists.\n- [`uifn/registry/src/preset/project.ts:136-149`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/75018c0db87b5b237eb375e78764a2ff3b2b67e1/uifn/registry/src/preset/project.ts#L136-L149) — full application always proposes `src/uifn-theme.css`.\n\n## Required outcome\n- A first apply must not overwrite an existing generated-output path unless ownership is already established.\n- Preserve the explicit consumer-manifest merge behavior.\n\n## Suggested approach\n- Reject differing existing files with no managed baseline, except paths handled by a dedicated merge operation, and add a first-apply collision test.\n````\n\n\u003c/details\u003e","line":213,"path":"uifn/registry/src/preset/project.ts"}
{"body":"This records `package.json` in the preset-managed hashes because only the state file is excluded. After a consumer edits its manifest, a later preset change that also adds a dependency is rejected as `UIFN_REGISTRY_DIRTY_CONFLICT`, contradicting the consumer-owned scripts and metadata contract.\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\u003csummary\u003eTechnical details\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n````markdown\n# Keep existing-project manifests consumer-owned\n\n## Affected sites\n- [`uifn/registry/src/preset/project.ts:61-77`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/75018c0db87b5b237eb375e78764a2ff3b2b67e1/uifn/registry/src/preset/project.ts#L61-L77) — serialization hashes every desired file except `.uifn/preset.json`.\n- [`uifn/registry/src/preset/project.ts:278-282`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/75018c0db87b5b237eb375e78764a2ff3b2b67e1/uifn/registry/src/preset/project.ts#L278-L282) — full apply adds the merged manifest before serializing state.\n- [`uifn/registry/docs/PRESET.md:54`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/75018c0db87b5b237eb375e78764a2ff3b2b67e1/uifn/registry/docs/PRESET.md#L54) — documents preservation of consumer scripts and metadata.\n\n## Required outcome\n- Consumer-owned manifest edits must survive later full applies, including applies that add or change preset dependencies.\n- Dirty-file protection should cover generator-owned files, not the whole manifest byte stream.\n\n## Suggested approach\n- Exclude the existing-project manifest from preset managed hashes, or track only the dependency entries owned by the preset, and add a reapply test after a consumer script edit.\n````\n\n\u003c/details\u003e","line":66,"path":"uifn/registry/src/preset/project.ts"}
